  "function_revised": "Secreted protein of the mycobacterial DUF732 family. All-vs-all structural clustering (Foldseek on ESMFold models, phase36) places it in a tight fold family (median TM-score 0.67) that includes the characterised host-directed effectors Rv1804c (sequesters host IkappaB-alpha) and Rv3354 (targets the host COP9 signalosome), plus the secreted antigen Rv1271c. It shares the family's N-terminal signal peptide (DeepTMHMM) and the ~110-aa secreted fold. A host-interaction / secreted-effector role is therefore plausible, but the specific molecular target of THIS member is not experimentally established (the DUF732 family is functionally heterogeneous).",
